# sandbox/pins.env — the versions the sandbox runs.
#
# A sandbox on a different Builder than the target is not a test bed, it is a
# second opinion from a stranger. Pin by COMMIT, never by branch, and never by
# the reported version string — see the note below, which is the whole reason
# this file is strict.

# --- Builder -----------------------------------------------------------------
#
# WHY A SHA AND NOT "v1.0.0-dev":
#
# `1.0.0-dev` is not a release. It is the placeholder version string carried by
# Builder's `develop` branch, set on 2025-12-12 (commit e6202e23, which replaced
# "1.18.0" with "1.0.0-dev"). Every develop commit since reports the same string
# — over a thousand of them. Within that one version string Builder has already:
#
#   2026-06-11  e12ca57b  ADDED    Builder Snapshot
#   2026-07-16  f0781da9  RENAMED  Builder Variable -> Builder Token  (refactor!)
#
# So "we target v1.0.0-dev" identifies nothing. Two sandboxes both honestly
# reporting `1.0.0-dev` can disagree about whether our entire token doctype
# exists. Pin the commit. Full story: ADR-004.
#
# CONFIRMED 2026-08-04, on the second attempt. The first answer (15cb01e4) was
# wrong by 55 commits and 17 days, and wrong in a believable way: it reported
# "433 of 435 blobs matched" and dismissed the residue. Against that commit the
# real figures are 87 files differing and 69 host-only — a match *rate* hid the
# answer, which is the same mistake as measuring a clone by declaration counts.
#
# This pin is 452 of 454 byte-identical, and each of the three residues was
# named and explained: a regenerated components.d.ts, a regenerated yarn.lock,
# and Vite output that git never tracked.
#
# Corroborated against things that are NOT the tree:
#   - LICENSE is MIT; Builder relicensed from AGPL-3.0 on 2026-07-16, so the
#     host is provably at or after that date. This alone disproves 15cb01e4.
#   - the served templates/generators/webpage.html blob brackets the commit to
#     [2026-07-18, 2026-07-26)
#   - the image was created 2026-07-21T09:43Z, and develop HEAD at that instant
#     was exactly this commit
#
# Tree caveat, stated rather than glossed: tree 3fd08ae9 is shared by this merge
# and its second parent fc33913c. They are content-indistinguishable; this is the
# develop-line commit a `--branch develop` clone lands on.
BUILDER_REF=b09a40d98590d9c5eac91a9a9de1795edf364eec
BUILDER_REF_STATUS=confirmed            # provisional | confirmed
BUILDER_REPO=https://github.com/frappe/builder
BUILDER_BRANCH=develop                  # lineage, for the initial clone only

# Tracks upstream for evaluating an upgrade (ADR-003). Deliberately a branch:
# this pin is meant to move.
BUILDER_UPSTREAM_REF=develop

# --- Frappe ------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# CONFIRMED 2026-08-04: frappe 16.27.1, tag v16.27.1 on `version-16`. The tree
# match is exact — 3317 files, zero differences either way — so unlike the
# Builder pin there is no ambiguity here at all.
#
# Previously recorded as 16.25.0 (9a8daf34), which was also wrong. And before
# that this sandbox ran 17.x.x-develop, a pairing that exists nowhere.
FRAPPE_REF=f33ac3f00ab818e21b25ddbec93efb653fd9aa1b
FRAPPE_REF_STATUS=confirmed
FRAPPE_REPO=https://github.com/frappe/frappe
FRAPPE_BRANCH=version-16                # lineage, for the initial clone only

# --- Site --------------------------------------------------------------------
SITE_NAME=sandbox.localhost
ADMIN_PASSWORD=admin
DB_ROOT_PASSWORD=123
